"watch":"The signs in the brackets are the opposite of the centre’s coordinates.<br><br><b>Problem-solving lens</b><br>Group the x-terms and the y-terms, then complete each square on its own.","qs":[{"text":"A circle has centre (0; 0) and passes through (3; 4). Find r².","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"r²","a":"25","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"r is the distance from the centre to the point.","steps":"1. Formula (circle): (x − a)² + (y − b)² = r² has centre (a; b) and radius r. Complete the square in x and in y to get this form.<br>2. r² = 3² + 4² = 9 + 16<br>3. = 25"},{"text":"A circle has centre (1; 2) and passes through (4; 6). Find r².","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"r²","a":"25","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"r is the distance from the centre to the point.","steps":"1. Formula (circle): (x − a)² + (y − b)² = r² has centre (a; b) and radius r. Complete the square in x and in y to get this form.<br>2. r² = (4 − 1)² + (6 − 2)² = 9 + 16<br>3. = 25"},{"text":"Find the radius of x² + y² = 25.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Radius","a":"5","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"The equation is x² + y² = r².","steps":"1. Formula (circle): (x − a)² + (y − b)² = r² has centre (a; b) and radius r. Complete the square in x and in y to get this form.<br>2. x² + y² = 25 = 5², so r = 5"}]}